{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502930-campaign-brainstorming-help-what-can-wipe-out-covenants","id":1502930,"title":"[Campaign brainstorming help] What can wipe out Covenants ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-13T07:50:52-08:00","id":1502930,"title":"[Campaign brainstorming help] What can wipe out Covenants ?","content":"So has to not hijack the Ask a Simple Question thread, I've decided to build up my own thread to better devise a reason for the disappearance of two Covenants with entranched power bases : the Invictus and the LeS.<br /> <br /> Before anything else, the basics of the campaign as envisionned : it take places in the metropolitan area of Toulouse, so roughly 1M peoples in several connected towns.<br /> <br /> The remaining Covenants are Ordo Dracul and Carthians, united in an uneasy but somewhat stable alliance called the Vampiric University of Toulouse (The Ordo is dominant because of the Carthians being more fractious and two more Vampires in the Ordo).<br /> <br /> Of the twenty Vampires in the agreed upon borders of the &quot;University&quot; the repartition is as follow :<ul><li>9 Ordo Dracul (1 Elder Daeva who is the &quot;Prince&quot;; 1 Elder Ventrue; 3 Ancilla Mekhet; 1 Daeva Neonate, 2 Ventrue Neonate and 1 Nosferatu Neonate)</li> <li>7 Carthians (2 Ancilla Nosferatu; 1 Ventrue Ancilla; 1 Daeva Ancilla; 2 Daeva Neonate and 1 Ventrue Neonate)</li> <li>4 Independant : an Elder Gangrel, her Ancilla Childe and her Neonate Grand-Childe + 1 Nosferatu Ancilla</li> </ul>As you can see not that many young bloods or elders, especially for a 2000 + years old city. Of course some events have probably depopulated the region somewhat (Albigensian Crusade, Black Death, etc.).<br /> <br /> Still, what kind of event may have had affected the town to wipe out the Invictus and the Lancea et Sanctum (the Circle is basically non-existent in my mind in the South of France) ?<br /> <br /> It probably has to have happened during WWII and be terrible but still containable enough that some - by then - ancillas managed to held the town long enough to forge the alliance still clinging to power today<br /> <br /> But I really can't make up my mind on those events and how they have defined the culture of the local Covenants.<br /> <br /> So fellow Kindred -or Kine - your help would be much appreciated !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T06:26:19-08:00","id":1503020,"title":"","content":"Is the relationship between the Ordo and the Carthians bad? <br /> If so, I would propose a Carthian insurrection, which was to be supported by the Ordo. Instead, the Ordo Elder once the Lancea Prince and their cronies were gone, crowned themselves Prince and took some of the Invictus Ancilla under their wing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T06:44:21-08:00","id":1503022,"title":"","content":"In my mind it's not bad because they are allied but it's more of a &quot;our cultures are so different it's still kind of hard to work with you sometimes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Especially because the Carthians are devided between 4 &quot;Spaniards&quot; Vampiric Anarcho-Syndicalists and 3 &quot;French&quot; Statists so the Ordo has to consider how to bring them all over to its side for the planned developement of the Kindred here.<br /> <br /> What I know for sure I want for the event :<ul><li>It involved all four of the Covenants</li> <li>It happened during WWII</li> <li>It was brutal, leaving even the Ordo and Carthians reeling after their win</li> <li>The arrival of Spanish Carthians and perhaps one Dracul played a part in the ignition of the tensions</li> <li>Whatever it was, it was fast enough that reinforcements couldn't come from the nearby cities</li> </ul>With the difficulty being largely : what could lead to a wipe out of the Invictus and the Leanca instead of simply usurping their position of power ? So it has, at least to me, to be tied to a mundane AND metaphysical cause, something which meant that those two Covenants were so compromised that even Elders and Ancilla in the others two were willing to risk their unlives to get rid of the threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 02-14-2023, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T07:36:43-08:00","id":1503027,"title":"","content":"I guess there is always a nasty Strix then. Maybe it took over one the Covenant leaders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T08:55:09-08:00","id":1503036,"title":"","content":"The Strix may be a great adjuvant, certainly. I'm toying with the idea of one being kept trapped way below the Ordo's main research center, but it may not be enough.<br /> <br /> Here's the rough sketch I've thought over today, but not sure it makes much sense :<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Toulouse and the surrounding region experience a massive awakening of old Vampires a twenty years before WWII, considerably swelling the ranks of the Lancea and Invictus - among them one Strix-possessed. With so many Vampires, feeding becomes difficult and tensions rise quickly.</li> <li>New, more repressive policies were imposed by the ruling Covenants, subtly led astray by the Bird of Dis : Carthians weren't made illegal per se because the more modern Invictus and LeS didn't want an all out war, but Ordo Draculs had to officially disband - in practice they got ready for a fight if their illegal practices were discovered.</li> <li>Carthians from Spain came over and settled in the ara, considerably reinforcing the Carthians but also leading to a secession from Ligues (far-right militia) oriented Carthians who decided to use the rampant fascism and &quot;revival&quot; of old Vampires as a template, and formally defected, forming their own &quot;Covenant&quot;, the Ligue des Croix de Sang. The Strix adds kindling to the fire by rpeaching against &quot;enemies of the Blood&quot; in the ranks of Unaligned (in truth Ordo) vampires.</li> <li>With experience on their side, the Carthians knows what's coming and they rush to ally not only with the Ordo but also with true Unaligned, a Gangrel brood and a Nosferatu Elder and his Neonate. The tenets of the alliance still ruling Toulouse and the surrounding area is hammered out.</li> <li>Tensions boil over with the defeat of France and the rise of Vichy. The purges start inside the very two leading Covenant, as the &quot;ti\u00e8de&quot; are slaughtered to make way to true devoted, Night of Long Knives style. But just as the Invictus and Lancea finishes that night, they are brutally assaulted by the Carthians, who uses suicidal tactics by dragging their opponents in the fire and the sun.</li> <li>The next few nights, all out war break out, as Kindred, Militia, Resistance and a few other beings descends on each other in an orgy of violence. The Croix de Sang are espcially nasty but few in numbers and are singled out by the Firebrands, who wipe them out, at great cost.</li> <li>With mounting losses and their lack of Blood Sorcery, the Invictus tries to sue for peace, but the Strix then makes it moves, slaughtering the envoy and pretending that the Carthians did that, so the Invictus believed itself forced to fight to the bitter end.</li> <li>Meanwhile, the Ordo Dracul tries to ransack the accumulated knowledge of the Lancea et Sanctum, whose archives stretches back to early Christianism era in the region. The Dragons and the Spears wage a particularly savage battle, but their initial purge has weakened the Lance enough that the Dragons finishes them off, wanting to preserve their monopoly on the archive's knowledge.</li> <li>The last Invictus are slain as the Strix reveal himself. The Carthians retreat but the Kogaion of the Ordo &quot;destroys&quot; it.</li> </ol><br /> Does it seem plausible for Vampires to go to such lengths to des troy each others ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T13:12:50-08:00","id":1503058,"title":"","content":"I don't know.... Ok, the kindred population was larger before things went pear-shaped big time leading to the destruction of the local Invictus and Sanctified, but that timeline feels too &quot;top down big politics&quot; for an urban area with what, 30-50 kindred in it's heyday? Some public schools can have classes larger than that depending on one's country or region.<br /> <br /> Makes me think &quot;politics&quot; would be far more personal and clique-ish, because it ain't hard to know, or at least know about, all local kindred and to interact with them on a personal level.<br /> <br /> In current Toulouse as described just the average 4-5 PCs coterie would mean a 20-25% rise in kindred population. That makes &quot;factionalism&quot; somewhat more questionable i dare say.<br /> <br /> Also, clan/brood lines can matter even more in this setting due to these small numbers - who's whose sire, who was embraced by kindred now torpid or destroyed, who came already undead to the city from messes in other domains?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T01:09:45-08:00","id":1503116,"title":"","content":"I need to flesh out the lineages indeed !<br /> <br /> It'll help adds the personal recriminations which played a huge part in the tensions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T03:04:46-08:00","id":1503123,"title":"","content":"Well, let's take a 2nd look at Toulouse's contemporary kindred population then:<br /> <br /> - Daeva: 1 Elder Dragon (the &quot;Prince&quot;); 1 Carthian Ancilla; 2 Carthian Neonates; 1 Neonate Dragon<br /> - Gangrel (All Unaligned): 1 Elder, her Ancilla Childe and Neonate Grand-Childe<br /> - Mekhet: 3 Dragon Ancillae;<br /> - Nosferatu: 2 Carthian Ancillae; 1 Unaligned Ancilla; 1 Neonate Dragon;<br /> - Ventrue: 1 Elder Dragon; 1 Carthian Ancilla; 2 Neonate Dragons; 1 Carthian Neonate;<br /> <br /> That is interesting on its own by showing the Gangrel may be seen as kind of insular and an understated faction of its own, since the Unaligned/Independents might as well not exist if not for them, who were the most clearly thought as a family nucleus.\u200b<br /> <br /> The Mekhet are also very curious in that all three of those in the city are dragons <b>and </b>ancillae <b>both</b>. No precursors, no descendants, all of them established in the mid rungs so to speak of the same group.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, what counts as ancilla for the standards of the kindred in the domain - 50-150 years of unlife, 100-200 years?<br /> What is the measure of an elder, 150+, 200-300, 300+ years? These things can help framing how much knowledge or not do the available NPCs have of the city's history, mundane, secret or occult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-15-2023, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T05:00:52-08:00","id":1503131,"title":"","content":"For this campaing the age classes are basically as follow :<ul><li>Elders = 150+ years</li> <li>Ancilla = 50-150 years</li> <li>Neonate= 0-50 years</li> </ul>Regarding the Mekhet, I'm thinking about making them the Childe of the previous Kogaion, who survived the events, while their Sire died/fell to torpor/serves as a prison for the Strix. All three are devoted to their researches and hasn't Sired - yet.<br /> <br /> For the Gangrels I'm toying with the idea of either a lone elder who came in after the event, earned the right to Embrace because she can easily travel outside the city's limits and in exchange of neutrality and her role as a watcher of the borders, she's been granted entire amnisty from whatever drove her away from her ancient lands and the right to sire. I think I'll make here a very ancient one, who arose from torpor around around WWII. <br /> <br /> Or a by then Neonate who managed to rouse her Lady ftom torpor to protect their territories at the outskirts and sonce no one wants it and the Gangrel are happy to stay away from politics, nobody bothers telling them what to do, as long as they pay lip service to the &quot;Prince&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T06:34:37-08:00","id":1503136,"title":"","content":"A betrayal from within could do considerable damage to any organisation.<br /> Since the Invitus is built on trust that those at the top will keep their promises also if the wars lead to a reduction in available feeding they could have been discredited.<br /> edit: It should be noted that the Carthians are often hinted or stated to have benefited from the Revaluation in a big way but that\u2019s probably more relevant in the North.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 02-15-2023, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T07:03:55-08:00","id":1503137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502930-campaign-brainstorming-help-what-can-wipe-out-covenants?p=1503131#post1503131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For this campaing the age classes are basically as follow :<ul><li>Elders = 150+ years</li> <li>Ancilla = 50-150 years</li> <li>Neonate= 0-50 years</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Good, now we have a framework to maybe tinker those events/flashpoints within. Is the chronicle set in the present, turn of the millenium or last decades of the 20th century?<br /> <br /> Because the spanish civil war is bordering 85+ years in the past, depending if one counts from its begining or end. Add about a decade if one counts the rise of fascist-style movements in Europe.<br /> Meaning almost half the Carthian membership <i>wasn't even around</i> the period or the following decade, for example - at least in a game set in the present.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502930-campaign-brainstorming-help-what-can-wipe-out-covenants?p=1503131#post1503131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Mekhet, I'm thinking about making them the Childe of the previous Kogaion, who survived the events, while their Sire died/fell to torpor/serves as a prison for the Strix. All three are devoted to their researches and hasn't Sired - yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> They could be all part of a brood, or not - in fact, 50-150 years is a quite respectable and yet diverse timeframe. It would be perfectly possible to have a sire-childer duo in different points of the same &quot;tier&quot;, with a childe embraced during WW2 by an older vampire that remembers <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_French_Empire#The_empire&#39;s_end\" target=\"_blank\">the waning years of the Second Empire</a>.<br /> Both would count as &quot;ancilla&quot; and yet be products of much different epochs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502930-campaign-brainstorming-help-what-can-wipe-out-covenants?p=1503131#post1503131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Gangrels I'm toying with the idea of either a lone elder who came in after the event, earned the right to Embrace because she can easily travel outside the city's limits and in exchange of neutrality and her role as a watcher of the borders, she's been granted entire amnisty from whatever drove her away from her ancient lands and the right to sire. I think I'll make here a very ancient one, who arose from torpor around around WWII.<br /> <br /> Or a by then Neonate who managed to rouse her Lady ftom torpor to protect their territories at the outskirts and sonce no one wants it and the Gangrel are happy to stay away from politics, nobody bothers telling them what to do, as long as they pay lip service to the &quot;Prince&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a bit of both perhaps?<br /> <br /> And either way, you picked a city, so <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toulouse#History\" target=\"_blank\">try to immerse yourself in the enviroment</a> to see what ideas and twists may come out.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T07:13:40-08:00","id":1503138,"title":"","content":"Honestly in a city of 50 vampires it\u2019s not impossible that there just wasn\u2019t enough interest for one or more of the Covenants to form. With no circle that\u2019s an average of 12 vampires or about 3 coteries per covenant minus unaligned, once the fighting begins the fair weather members will jump ship so 5 kills could be enough to eliminate a covenant (once the Bishop and his second in command are gone what\u2019s left of the Lancea et Sanctum? Probably not enough to organise an offensive), you\u2019re pretty much playing rocket tag so an early loss could take you out of the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 02-15-2023, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T08:43:33-08:00","id":1503141,"title":"","content":"Okay so I did a basic diagram of who's linked to whom to better grasp the relationships, I'll add to it has ideas flow : <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1V64HBDwQS5xPg5al8Ki5uTOHhcidWn5a/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1V64...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T11:31:48-08:00","id":1503465,"title":"","content":"What happened to the Camarilla in Requiem for Rome?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:39:19-08:00","id":1503480,"title":"","content":"Same thing that happened to Rome; it collapsed.<br /> <br /> Outside the sourcebook &quot;Fall of the Camarilla,&quot; it's left rather vague. The Strix were involved, somehow. VII might have been involved, too. The Julii were wiped out, as far as everyone knows, and most of the Camarilla power structure vanished with them. Then the Ventrue suddenly appeared shortly after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T14:32:44-08:00","id":1503491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502930-campaign-brainstorming-help-what-can-wipe-out-covenants?p=1503138#post1503138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly in a city of 50 vampires it\u2019s not impossible that there just wasn\u2019t enough interest for one or more of the Covenants to form. With no circle that\u2019s an average of 12 vampires or about 3 coteries per covenant minus unaligned, once the fighting begins the fair weather members will jump ship so 5 kills could be enough to eliminate a covenant (once the Bishop and his second in command are gone what\u2019s left of the Lancea et Sanctum? Probably not enough to organise an offensive), you\u2019re pretty much playing rocket tag so an early loss could take you out of the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much agree on this. A kindred population in the low tens is not going to be able to sustain much in the way of factionalism, be it in the form of covenants wjat to say ot cliques and internal divisions between them, on its own except perhaps as part of greater regional movements or networks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T06:09:30-08:00","id":1503678,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay in answer, I've been quite busy.<br /> <br /> Just to clear up something, the actual number of Vampires in Toulouse is really low in the modern era, basically what it was at the end of the XIXth because of severla factors :<ul><li>The event which wiped out two Covenants</li> <li>A political will from the surviving Vampires, relatively young at that time, to drastically control Embraces, so as to better cement their rules and have a better idea of who's who in the limits of the metropolitan area</li> <li>The easiness to move from one City to another in France (a lot of night train, low distance between big cities, etc.) allowed some Vampires to simply flee</li> <li>Torpor plays a large role (there is several examples provided in the diagram of lineages) because several of the old vampires who woke up, saw the shit-show going on and decided that, in the end, a century in torpor on top of another wasn't, in fact, that bad</li> </ul>It's also a low number of Vamps because creating fully-fledged NPCs takes a lot of time - knowing me, there will be more on the fly over the campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T19:39:25-08:00","id":1503722,"title":"","content":"Also, the Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}